{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/343194-token-pistol-in-faerie","id":343194,"title":"Token: Pistol in Faerie?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-17T13:52:03-08:00","id":343194,"title":"Token: Pistol in Faerie?","content":"My player very much like to have Colt Python pistol from his life before the Durance to still work in Arcadia. I know that most mechanism in Faerie do not work, but I agreed with this as Token. Question is - how much would it cost as Merit? What could be a Drawback?<br /> <br /> For now I said to him that this Colt work in Arcadia, but it will needs to use hand forged iron bullets. And that it stings a user, as he will dealt Aggravated damage to all fae. Is it logical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T14:18:30-08:00","id":343253,"title":"","content":"You're the storyteller, you're the one who should set these things as appropriate. And for the record, cold iron deals lethal to True Fae, while cold forged iron deals aggravated, at least in first edition. So good luck making bullets of cold forged iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T14:22:14-08:00","id":343269,"title":"","content":"Hand-forged iron in a Token? Sounds risky. I don't recall anything in the rule forbidding it, but it's good to keep in mind iron tears through faerie defenses. That could inform the pistol's drawback though--perhaps every time it's fired, roll a chance die. On a normal failure, the iron bullet fucks up the Token's Glamour enough to require repair before it can be used again (otherwise there's a cumulative -1 penalty to the shooting roll). On a dramatic failure, the gun's gone forever. Maybe it just falls apart like a bundle of sticks, maybe it explodes in the user's hand. Whatever seems more appropriate.<br /> <br /> In <i>Autumn Nightmares</i>, there's a Fae who possesses a Token pistol that shoots plant seeds instead of bullets; the wounds it inflicts bloom with swiftly-growing flowers. If you need some inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T20:15:53-08:00","id":343606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/343194-token-pistol-in-faerie?p=343269#post343269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand-forged iron in a Token? Sounds risky. I don't recall anything in the rule forbidding it, but it's good to keep in mind iron tears through faerie defenses. That could inform the pistol's drawback though--perhaps every time it's fired, roll a chance die. On a normal failure, the iron bullet fucks up the Token's Glamour enough to require repair before it can be used again (otherwise there's a cumulative -1 penalty to the shooting roll). On a dramatic failure, the gun's gone forever. Maybe it just falls apart like a bundle of sticks, maybe it explodes in the user's hand. Whatever seems more appropriate.<br /> <br /> In <i>Autumn Nightmares</i>, there's a Fae who possesses a Token pistol that shoots plant seeds instead of bullets; the wounds it inflicts bloom with swiftly-growing flowers. If you need some inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Autumn Nightmares also includes a milestone Merit that makes a fetchbane token out of the murder implement, which explicitly can't be applied to cold-iron weapons.<br /> <br /> Important thing to know about any given mechanism's viability in Faerie: to borrow a phrase from Garth Nix, it's fashion. If a Fae's given domain is hosting a narrative where guns are a thing (e.g. alien gangster noir), guns will work in some capacity. If, as many of them do instead, the place is running something closer to medieval-era fairy-tale witch/feudal-lord stories, the odds are rather lower. Everything's up in the air in any given part of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T11:20:49-08:00","id":344003,"title":"","content":"I think even Valkyrie's Mjolnir Cannon would work in the Realm of my Fae that has cyborg arm shooting sunlight in spite of him ruling his court like out of Arthurian legends. He is quite an oddball even in comparison to other Fae.<br /> <br /> This is my little nod to the fact that The Elder Scrolls' Pelinal &quot;Star Made Knight / Divine Crusader&quot; Whitestrake was actually a cyborg with an arm of &quot;killing light&quot; in a setting supposedly to be pre-modern, Dwemer notwithstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 12-18-2014, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}